EXPERIMENT 58 – SESSION MANAGEMENT AND COOKIE HANDLING USING APACHE JMETER
AIM
To use Apache JMeter to test session management and cookie handling using the HTTP Cookie Manager.
ALGORITHM
1. Start Apache JMeter and rename the Test Plan.
2. Add a Thread Group.
3. Set Threads = 3, Ramp-up = 3 seconds and Loop Count = 1.
4. Add HTTP Cookie Manager.
5. Add HTTP Request POST /authenticate with valid login details and select Follow Redirects.
6. Add HTTP Request GET /secure.
7. Add Response Assertion to the second request with pattern Welcome to the Secure Area.
8. Run the test with Cookie Manager enabled.
9. Disable Cookie Manager and run again.
10. Compare both results to understand session handling.
INPUT
Element	Property	Value
Thread Group	Threads	3
Thread Group	Ramp-up	3 seconds
Thread Group	Loop Count	1
HTTP Cookie Manager	Run 1	Enabled
HTTP Cookie Manager	Run 2	Disabled
HTTP Request 1	Server	the-internet.herokuapp.com
HTTP Request 1	Method / Path	POST /authenticate
Parameters	Username	tomsmith
Parameters	Password	SuperSecretPassword!
HTTP Request 2	Method / Path	GET /secure
Response Assertion	Pattern	Welcome to the Secure Area

OUTPUT
Run 1 – Cookie Manager Enabled
Label	Samples	Error %
POST /authenticate	3	0.00%
GET /secure	3	0.00%

Run 2 – Cookie Manager Disabled
Label	Samples	Error %
POST /authenticate	3	0.00%
GET /secure	3	100.00%

Without the Cookie Manager, the session is lost and the login page is returned.
RESULT
Thus, Apache JMeter was used to test session management and cookie handling using the HTTP Cookie Manager, and the results were verified.
